  <context>
    <background>Cancellation reason: the owner chose option C on 2026-11-07 (notes/decisions.md 2026-11-07; spec FR-10 as amended, which supersedes design §8 B-4). In ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore 2.3.1 the stateless transport runs MCP tool handlers inside the ASP.NET request: StreamableHttpHandler passes context.RequestServices with ScopeRequests=false, and the default PerSessionExecutionContext=false keeps IHttpContextAccessor working. MCP tools therefore read the request HttpContext through IHttpContextAccessor and call the decision services unchanged, including DecisionPlanReadStamp, DecisionParameterSources, DecisionActionExecutors, DecisionRouteCores, AssignTaskNotifier, DecisionCommitFollowUps and BudgetInquiryExecutor. Threading ICallerContext through those files is no longer needed, and neither is the source-scan guard this task would have added. Task 010 now verifies the MCP caller path with tests instead. Former dependants: 017 now depends on 011 only.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/decisions.md (2026-11-07 option C entry)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/tasks/010-mcp-caller-path-verification.poml (the replacement verification)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">Cancelled; no prerequisite applies.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

